[{:db/id "q-163206/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "39fc179d-d5f9-5758-ba76-aef66997b099" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b31b02f2-6f0f-5be1-bebc-5352286bfa39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "eac26a23-34e9-524a-a047-9d483949abf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "daa97450-83f2-52b0-a7a0-732b002eb158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "c3c8e3b4-fadc-5ec4-be54-c0e70978a13e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0df1b95-e683-53b1-9b1d-a4ca3e1a5c9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163206/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-163206/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-163206/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163206/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163206/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-163206/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163206" :question/id #uuid "07500176-d029-58d8-93f9-f1b431357d71" :question/math-academy-id "q-163206" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x+2y,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(2x+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[2xy+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{x}^{2}+4x]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {2}^{2}+4\\cdot 2)-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=2.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =f(a,2)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 16 & =(2a+2\\cdot 2)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 4 & =2a+4 \\\\ 0 & =2a \\\\ a & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(0,2)\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $a=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163206/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163206"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5a1688a3-9e6c-5505-aa46-444fdce3b7e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "2a2255ff-2eee-5576-83ba-4df11643b384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "a374ad7b-4037-5fe5-a477-1e23b9d73485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1d1898d6-5be9-5fb5-bfa8-c236f5906511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "07839f96-468c-5f13-a02a-057066e75c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "351c7399-da34-5bf2-b03c-007352d08b71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163207/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-163207/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-163207/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-163207/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163207/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163207/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163207" :question/id #uuid "32cb59f5-2cfc-5591-af91-5e27d57635d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-163207" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x+y,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $b$ given that $a=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3x+\\frac{9}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{9x}{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\cdot (3)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{9\\cdot (3)}{2})-0 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=3\\cdot 3=9.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $a=2.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27 & =f(2,b)\\cdot 9 \\\\ 27 & =(2+b)\\cdot 9 \\\\ 27 & =9b+18 \\\\ 9 & =9b \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(2,1)\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $b=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163207/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163207"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163059"] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}+2y+1,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $b$ given that $a=1.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+2y+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}+2y+1)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}+y]_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+12x]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =({2}^{3}+12\\cdot 2)-0 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $a=1.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32 & =f(1,b)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 32 & =({1}^{2}+2b+1)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 32 & =12b+12 \\\\ 20 & =12b \\\\ b & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(1,\\frac{5}{3})\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $b=\\frac{5}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "284e3b2a-af8d-54a1-a964-38459a601ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "935509bc-a7cf-572f-a823-496d9491c672" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "266cdf9b-29cc-5291-b75d-692f0e0c5709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "375a4d93-8e93-5e45-aa33-a9d49e7ea962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "cf670a77-e7c5-56e6-8294-8ee46f1d311b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "afed27b5-6510-5b47-ad11-b1c5764da520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163153/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-163153/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163153/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163153/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-163153/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" "q-163153/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163153" :question/id #uuid "66733011-5928-5fa9-9d1c-b24200b7104a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163153" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x+4y,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=1.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(2x+4y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}(2x+4y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[2xy+2{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}12{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[4{x}^{3}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=1.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32 & =f(a,1)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 32 & =(2a+4\\cdot 1)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 8 & =2a+4 \\\\ 4 & =2a \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(2,1)\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $a=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5789f9a4-5b59-5b4c-89f7-40353cdc3ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "7ffd6da2-11f0-56aa-94c4-18c7fec19c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "4fc12df6-f41d-56bb-be32-f9482f163cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "768c5288-b88c-5647-bc21-e705786d2cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "9ccc8ff1-323b-57bd-bbec-c316ccf57c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "08b4c578-30b6-54d1-bc0c-bb2968e8b6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163148/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-163148/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-163148/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-163148/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-163148/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-163148/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163148" :question/id #uuid "b06b29a8-f2f2-551a-aa07-dc58db5a1ae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163148" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=6{x}^{2}-2y+2,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $b$ given that $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b)\\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=f(a,b)\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(6{x}^{2}-2y+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{x}^{2}-2y+2)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[6{x}^{2}y-{y}^{2}+2y]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{x}^{3}+x]_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {1}^{3}+1)-(2\\cdot (-1)^{3}+(-1)) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =f(\\frac{1}{2},b)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 6 & =(6\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2b+2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{7}{2}-2b \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & =-2b \\\\ b & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4})\\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $b=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163148/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d13b0d31-65b8-550f-b97b-f4ece63bf834"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "bbdd2889-f4ce-55b1-9e0e-4ea6cff9b807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "87395c66-2072-5995-ace4-dd1243a5b877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "35ebd65b-e875-5b56-9666-b85f4af6ba3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "6d887425-acc0-5615-8335-98ed92c7b638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9dedcc09-df3f-558e-bc6c-76af98360cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a1701e8-86e9-59a1-b366-770d392db03c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163246/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-163246/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-163246/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-163246/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-163246/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-163246/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163246" :question/id #uuid "dc061799-2611-580f-81d1-666b5e54d90b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163246" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=2x+3{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}(2x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2xy+{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2{x}^{2}+8x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot {1}^{2}+8\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163246/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163246"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "0b9f897a-f43e-5533-b27a-0c7d246f65e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3cc662b9-0167-5a65-9528-9c7880916e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d0e228f5-3120-5474-b93c-9feafa863af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection/787ba90009a2104196393a6fa203fa7646fc82176685c8ab9f72d2176e83792a" :answer/id #uuid "d5f775a3-32ed-5019-ab86-e50a76a13cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "bded0ac4-1a3d-56b3-9e69-f63df4a40b52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c032b66-d2dd-5d13-9ed3-135a693ec13a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163235/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-163235/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-163235/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-163235/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-163235/selection/787ba90009a2104196393a6fa203fa7646fc82176685c8ab9f72d2176e83792a" "q-163235/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163235" :question/id #uuid "34aa98cf-6792-50ad-a573-1705f95f8787" :question/math-academy-id "q-163235" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+6{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 1=2.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}({x}^{3}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{3}y+2{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+2x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+2\\cdot 2-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163235/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163235"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f25a59c0-056a-5701-8674-d62c4236d41b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "c7162db5-fa1f-5fb3-8140-af1dacdf19c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "f9efc787-dd43-5075-83a6-4e07660f1f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "7aadc05e-1c3d-5b8e-9d65-8601a5a1a0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "bb7c0c82-6968-5d42-b461-dc21d47c6c46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "04b2384c-8bb8-5828-8551-6425e611cdaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163241/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-163241/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-163241/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-163241/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-163241/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-163241/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163241" :question/id #uuid "c780d3a5-445d-5711-8c66-c3ce378a6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163241" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x+3{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le x+1}$ given that the area of the region is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}x+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{x+1}x+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[xy+{y}^{3}]_{y=x}^{y=x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3{x}^{2}+4x+1]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+x]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18-0) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163241/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9112772d-31ff-578a-a582-e2b4beee94cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "ce8ed80a-9a9c-55f6-92e4-2e4e59a536c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "b5896e91-ed14-5b39-b2a7-654c250e40ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6d99e78b-b59b-5613-9f94-1345266d7296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "302fc955-4607-596d-ae98-c1e5f8ecbfe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3873d4-a0c7-5879-a8fb-662ae99c510b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163255/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-163255/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-163255/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-163255/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-163255/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-163255/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163255" :question/id #uuid "47c72fc7-8dae-51ee-b86c-f302860768d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163255" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=12x{y}^{3}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{4}}$ given that the area of the region is $\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}{∬}_{D}12x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x/4}12x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3x{y}^{4}]_{y=0}^{y=x/4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{256}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{512}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{8}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163255/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163255"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-163063"] :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-4{y}^{3}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 3=3.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-4{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-4{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{x}^{2}y-{y}^{4}]_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}-81)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{x}^{3}-81x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-81\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{80}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection/f479715f25cdc89e876c210e1d5dd6850de641202a26b7cfcbcec1dae6f5ea5b" :answer/id #uuid "83abd66f-e6d9-5507-8525-b2dfd54ee777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" :answer/id #uuid "bb480b28-7db7-5899-ac11-6dc9a9e63e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection/d7751494ea03b36a0e6d708686a98190c7b28f086ef62e5550aba293fe070353" :answer/id #uuid "35db5483-83bf-5ea1-b7b2-fd34aab6d2fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection/62404fa2a3befdbadced522181a75c40bde39f599622d4f84a756feaa05ecb06" :answer/id #uuid "923f1a2e-61f6-5ce5-b298-42737b213b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection/7d5cb2f332b3f301a23fe106d8ba723a7bd83bf838e8df1d59ab973ad8f00e0d" :answer/id #uuid "9f4dd30e-4d66-5dd4-9144-96a0427bf510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0e9ce81-bfe0-57e1-8d36-9cf6fb4c3d3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163261/selection/d7751494ea03b36a0e6d708686a98190c7b28f086ef62e5550aba293fe070353" :answer-field/choices ["q-163261/selection/f479715f25cdc89e876c210e1d5dd6850de641202a26b7cfcbcec1dae6f5ea5b" "q-163261/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" "q-163261/selection/d7751494ea03b36a0e6d708686a98190c7b28f086ef62e5550aba293fe070353" "q-163261/selection/62404fa2a3befdbadced522181a75c40bde39f599622d4f84a756feaa05ecb06" "q-163261/selection/7d5cb2f332b3f301a23fe106d8ba723a7bd83bf838e8df1d59ab973ad8f00e0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163261" :question/id #uuid "a64de922-97db-5342-bd59-124a21855af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163261" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x-y$ on the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $y\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/95faae88fb4909a86492e45101419fe872aeb1cc2eeabde9cf773c8f71d31fff.png)\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x-y\\,dA & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ){\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\frac{1}{3}{[{r}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{4}{3\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163261/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163261"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection/c058486308bb0cd78b37658ea80351ed079362c2d3fe4782019619d209f198f7" :answer/id #uuid "d27c59ad-75c0-538e-a1d6-8336fba5826f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection/8b018ac31da054f22e304d987b846053ceef11d2dd3d7e17ae52c125b1fb2745" :answer/id #uuid "0b83f1a4-44c6-53b4-823a-2e3bc47e62c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection/06bcafe2f4ad0ed76b06b7f51a5f3fd6dfa806ee12194d82f120333358a7b8e0" :answer/id #uuid "6fedc574-134b-5ce9-a0bb-4164b8145124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection/5f107484d35442bc30456660a29a239e6aa66914c88484fd1ae90f3e12261244" :answer/id #uuid "aeea9680-4b6d-55d7-a0b4-8921cd37db64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection/35a8668c8558370137d4ee488ed2991fa97edb221d0db9ac678594fa85d3aab2" :answer/id #uuid "52c6f4aa-6f07-506f-8bfa-bb7ecbdfa665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9249ec28-3403-5e26-b753-e08d68481013" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163260/selection/06bcafe2f4ad0ed76b06b7f51a5f3fd6dfa806ee12194d82f120333358a7b8e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-163260/selection/c058486308bb0cd78b37658ea80351ed079362c2d3fe4782019619d209f198f7" "q-163260/selection/8b018ac31da054f22e304d987b846053ceef11d2dd3d7e17ae52c125b1fb2745" "q-163260/selection/06bcafe2f4ad0ed76b06b7f51a5f3fd6dfa806ee12194d82f120333358a7b8e0" "q-163260/selection/5f107484d35442bc30456660a29a239e6aa66914c88484fd1ae90f3e12261244" "q-163260/selection/35a8668c8558370137d4ee488ed2991fa97edb221d0db9ac678594fa85d3aab2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163260" :question/id #uuid "e164d930-d843-5cfb-9760-b4974ed33be6" :question/math-academy-id "q-163260" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}$ on the portion of the disk of radius $3$ centered at the origin, where $x\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/25c1f00e588ddaa130f854d9f4e9dfe9b1158d7952a01bae8108ea4b94d3c347.png)\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{2}{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{2r}{{r}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)]_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡10-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡10{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡10[\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡10(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{2}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡10=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection/62404fa2a3befdbadced522181a75c40bde39f599622d4f84a756feaa05ecb06" :answer/id #uuid "d451367d-8e25-56d0-9000-933a0c1f1e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection/47c40afe6bbcbddca0e36819bfea415e931f8f4ccbda43d44a719da2878a45fc" :answer/id #uuid "80536cde-1922-59de-ab9d-88e0ad5e5062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection/0dbec4870e57573286a3b337231517a95e48a6378854240cef143d28f877d639" :answer/id #uuid "c2c6e8a8-164f-55c1-8138-a11b93bb9a48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection/87dcf7a936a1fc4a0d52aa911471ad7003396b7fcef4da5304c69f6e81981052" :answer/id #uuid "ccda1394-5b9c-540b-b6ca-a4a83d1ee0ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection/1c44c0b5729e9f75bd238a8a45d10e25ed6a0c434e39a8d52b2d803f5d4b3718" :answer/id #uuid "ce825d5c-4b2e-587e-acb6-cbfce522b867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd4a03d-aa52-53a9-8db2-911c87db0be8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163278/selection/47c40afe6bbcbddca0e36819bfea415e931f8f4ccbda43d44a719da2878a45fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-163278/selection/62404fa2a3befdbadced522181a75c40bde39f599622d4f84a756feaa05ecb06" "q-163278/selection/47c40afe6bbcbddca0e36819bfea415e931f8f4ccbda43d44a719da2878a45fc" "q-163278/selection/0dbec4870e57573286a3b337231517a95e48a6378854240cef143d28f877d639" "q-163278/selection/87dcf7a936a1fc4a0d52aa911471ad7003396b7fcef4da5304c69f6e81981052" "q-163278/selection/1c44c0b5729e9f75bd238a8a45d10e25ed6a0c434e39a8d52b2d803f5d4b3718"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163278" :question/id #uuid "720aa004-4171-547e-b7da-98f76cf90612" :question/math-academy-id "q-163278" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/f84a8fcd4ed668a6b94d5b084ade49dc8fc027feff4baea862e2feaf68221534.png)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ on the semicircle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(-1,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $y=\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =-2x \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta [\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ((-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{4}-{0}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{[-\\frac{{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta }{5}]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}({cos}^{5}⁡\\pi -{cos}^{5}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{8}{5\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection/0fc9e01a0ed927de823a69ffd840123490099d2f56e7ba9a6f7c9c1c2d5473e9" :answer/id #uuid "9b3f5be0-7d2f-5927-9d74-21926d832708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection/b70aae751b2c8b3e9e8a13d794a4d2996d95172e6176a2e8db9c2f456750b489" :answer/id #uuid "2bc94184-eea7-5d14-979d-70942aa37562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection/a319e2074b264fdb964c2b6eb43d32d763280e23b0599a55d545f0a58e6fea9e" :answer/id #uuid "c0863946-913f-5ca3-ac71-b8f4c9ad45d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "cad94019-00dd-53ef-80fd-47a33542ca7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9977d049-058f-561e-a2fc-77c1d66d1a61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0745ff6a-c932-5b1d-99b3-a3b2405d2c6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163279/selection/a319e2074b264fdb964c2b6eb43d32d763280e23b0599a55d545f0a58e6fea9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-163279/selection/0fc9e01a0ed927de823a69ffd840123490099d2f56e7ba9a6f7c9c1c2d5473e9" "q-163279/selection/b70aae751b2c8b3e9e8a13d794a4d2996d95172e6176a2e8db9c2f456750b489" "q-163279/selection/a319e2074b264fdb964c2b6eb43d32d763280e23b0599a55d545f0a58e6fea9e" "q-163279/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-163279/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163279" :question/id #uuid "22a142c9-9e75-53eb-93f7-728128a3ebf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163279" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/719f86db69489f62bcbe2753e88cdc6713f04dc6f53415cc2484e2eaab8ffac3.png)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ on the semicircle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(0,1).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $x=\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{2y-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2y-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }(2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -0)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}\\cdot 1=\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "bbd8c209-7ef8-5554-b9a9-8a1d6606913f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection/d7751494ea03b36a0e6d708686a98190c7b28f086ef62e5550aba293fe070353" :answer/id #uuid "fd683e0f-7256-5d86-9e8d-f9986f537182" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection/a2bf9f278822239fe980121e1c2efe6b2a1075aef929e587d78abba90e1e8b5d" :answer/id #uuid "b4745229-f1fd-5b4e-b09b-761fa24c8f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" :answer/id #uuid "3c2f28dc-7652-5601-b7e3-58ce8a327f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "dd19b945-73c0-5450-af87-979bc3399c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c062c7cf-706d-5043-8a02-50c9729b03cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163070/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-163070/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-163070/selection/d7751494ea03b36a0e6d708686a98190c7b28f086ef62e5550aba293fe070353" "q-163070/selection/a2bf9f278822239fe980121e1c2efe6b2a1075aef929e587d78abba90e1e8b5d" "q-163070/selection/593500a3db867a568918b2d1a5f966e5ba3cb22b6d2f65c83b20e9be1edb20e9" "q-163070/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163070" :question/id #uuid "b77b3c65-9b31-5270-b685-33cd0e1cb660" :question/math-academy-id "q-163070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/fd1a5a140c3a2d430312d6f6ceeb21d6b7282119c8ec53365553ff845d8c64d5.png)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ on the semicircle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\frac{1}{2}$ centered at \n$(0,-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $x=\\sqrt{-{y}^{2}-y}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{-{y}^{2}-y} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-{y}^{2}-y \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =-y \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}+r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 0}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta [\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ((-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{4}-{0}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡\\theta }{5}]}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}({sin}^{5}⁡(0)-{sin}^{5}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{20}=\\frac{2}{5\\pi }.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163070/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12490"] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)$ and the region $D$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y) =\\dfrac{xy}2, \\qquad\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2y, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nAccording to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b) \\in D$ such that the volume of the solid enclosed between the surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane over the region $D$ equals the volume of the right cylinder with base $D$ and height $f(a,b).$ Find $a$ given that $b=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the mean value theorem for double integrals, there exists a point $(a,b) \\in D$ such that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_D f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A = f(a,b) \\cdot \\textrm{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the integral on the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\frac{xy}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{4}]_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we are told that $b=2.$ So, our initial equation simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64 & =f(a,2)\\cdot 16 \\\\ 64 & =\\frac{a\\cdot 2}{2}\\cdot 16 \\\\ 64 & =16a \\\\ a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\left( 4,2 \\right) \\in D.$ Therefore, the answer is $a = 4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12491"] :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y) = xy$ on the region $D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: x \\leq y \\leq 3x \\big\\}$ given that the area of the region is $3$ square units." :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{3x}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}]_{y=x}^{y=3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{x}^{4}]_{x=-1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(16-1) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12492"] :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y) = 15xy^2$ on the portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at the origin, where $x\\geq 0,$ and $y \\leq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081614/assets/a381fede820f9fc5ba08bb9569906d41a3e8f779de38b446c4f271ceef3a5ccd.png)\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac\\pi 4.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{\\textrm{ave}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{Area}(D)} \\, \\iint\\limits_D f(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y) \\ \\mathrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(r\\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta) \\:  r \\ \\mathrm d r \\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r, \\theta),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\left\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\: \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2} \\leq \\theta \\leq 2\\pi\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}15r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}15{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}5{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{[{r}^{5}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ({1}^{5}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={[{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta ]}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =({sin}^{3}⁡(2\\pi )-{sin}^{3}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nf_{\\textrm{ave}} = \\dfrac{4}{\\pi} \\cdot 1 = \\dfrac{4}{\\pi}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
